(CLI-04: `--shared` - build a shared library (.so) instead of an
 executable. Also emits a companion `.lib` interface file next to the
 `.so` (undocumented in this section, but needed by CLI-05/CLI-06's
 `--link`/`--lib-path` and by the Libraries and Imports chapter's `see
 ... from "....lib"` consumption path). This probe's source is also an
 ordinary compilable program on its own (see the standard Ran: line
 below) - `--shared` is a build mode, not a different dialect of Vox.
 Hand-run separately:
   $ vox tally_lib.vox --shared -o libtally.so
   $ ls libtally.so libtally.lib
   libtally.lib
   libtally.so
   $ file libtally.so
   libtally.so: ELF 64-bit LSB shared object, x86-64, ...
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox CLI-04.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   42
)
Library tally version "1.0".

To 'double it' with a number called value. Return a number, value multiply 2.

a number called result is 'double it' of 21.
Print result.
